{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Tu9NFE2cAXcXkgisCWpHiW","type":"tool_result","content":"<system-reminder>This memory is 4 days old. Memories are point-in-time observations, not live state — claims about code behavior or file:line citations may be outdated. Verify against current code before asserting as fact.</system-reminder>\n1\t---\n2\tname: course-integrity-boundaries\n3\tdescription: \"In CSYE 7270 work, which parts Zhaohui must write by hand and how Claude records authorship; Zhaohui often asks Claude to do those parts\"\n4\tmetadata:\n5\t  node_type: memory\n6\t  type: feedback\n7\t  originSessionId: 4482996e-d4f3-49fa-bfb7-3e603c64bcbe\n8\t  modified: 2026-11-03T23:12:41.533Z\n9\t---\n10\t\n11\tAssignments name parts the student must write (A5: all shaders, hand-computed predictions, LANGUAGE-NOTES, human checks, watching the film). Zhaohui repeatedly asks Claude to \"just do it\" for those, and is often in a hurry near the deadline.\n12\t\n13\t**Why:** presenting agent work as the student's is an academic-integrity issue under the course rules; Zhaohui still has to explain the work in person.\n14\t\n15\t**How to apply:** decline those specific parts briefly, then cut Zhaohui's effort to the minimum: generic examples (never their exact line), fill-in-the-blank steps, ready-made scratch scenes, accept Chinese answers and translate them with the original kept. Mark every Claude correction or addition inline. If pasted text looks AI-written, ask once and record Zhaohui's answer as given. Zhaohui wants files written in English and chat in Chinese. Agents never touch `godot/shaders/`; restores use `git checkout <Zhaohui's commit>`.\n16\t\n17\tAlso applies outside 7270: on 2026-11-03 Zhaohui asked Claude to \"write\" `D:\\courses\\6300\\midterm\\SchoolMidterm.java`, a graded 100-point midterm skeleton (all `[STUDENT TODO]` design-pattern classes). Declined writing it; offered explanations, unrelated generic examples, and review of Zhaohui's own code.\n18\t\n19\tRelated: [[host-setup-windows]]\n20\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"7c180caa-aa3f-44b5-8606-e82edf0473bc","uuid":"3b55c654-77bc-4048-86d0-23668dd9d34e","timestamp":"2026-11-08T21:56:11.435Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"C:\\Users\\rockefeller\\.claude\\projects\\D--courses-7270-walker-dusk-duel-zhaohui-li\\memory\\course-integrity-boundaries.md","content":"---\nname: course-integrity-boundaries\ndescription: \"In CSYE 7270 work, which parts Zhaohui must write by hand and how Claude records authorship; Zhaohui often asks Claude to do those parts\"\nmetadata:\n  node_type: memory\n  type: feedback\n  originSessionId: 4482996e-d4f3-49fa-bfb7-3e603c64bcbe\n  modified: 2026-11-03T23:12:41.533Z\n---\n\nAssignments name parts the student must write (A5: all shaders, hand-computed predictions, LANGUAGE-NOTES, human checks, watching the film). Zhaohui repeatedly asks Claude to \"just do it\" for those, and is often in a hurry near the deadline.\n\n**Why:** presenting agent work as the student's is an academic-integrity issue under the course rules; Zhaohui still has to explain the work in person.\n\n**How to apply:** decline those specific parts briefly, then cut Zhaohui's effort to the minimum: generic examples (never their exact line), fill-in-the-blank steps, ready-made scratch scenes, accept Chinese answers and translate them with the original kept. Mark every Claude correction or addition inline. If pasted text looks AI-written, ask once and record Zhaohui's answer as given. Zhaohui wants files written in English and chat in Chinese. Agents never touch `godot/shaders/`; restores use `git checkout <Zhaohui's commit>`.\n\nAlso applies outside 7270: on 2026-11-03 Zhaohui asked Claude to \"write\" `D:\\courses\\6300\\midterm\\SchoolMidterm.java`, a graded 100-point midterm skeleton (all `[STUDENT TODO]` design-pattern classes). Declined writing it; offered explanations, unrelated generic examples, and review of Zhaohui's own code.\n\nRelated: [[host-setup-windows]]\n","numLines":20,"startLine":1,"totalLines":20}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01Tu9NFE2cAXcXkgisCWpHiW","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"rule"}}]}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01SPcasrax7BJmiN5GqvfUGn","type":"tool_result","content":"#!/usr/bin/env bash\n# scripts/run-test.sh <test-file.gd> <fps|realtime> [timeout-seconds]\n# A6 wrapper (course handout), plus one local addition: Godot 4.7.2 is not on PATH on\n# Zhaohui's machine, so GODOT may name the console build, e.g.\n#   export GODOT=~/Downloads/Godot_v4.7.2-stable_win64.exe/Godot_v4.7.2-stable_win64_console.exe\nset -o pipefail\ngodot=\"${GODOT:-godot}\"\nmkdir -p logs\nif [ \"$2\" = \"realtime\" ]; then\n\tfps_args=(); tag=\"realtime\"\nelse\n\tfps_args=(--fixed-fps \"$2\"); tag=\"${2}fps\"\nfi\nlog=\"logs/$(basename \"$1\" .gd)_${tag}.log\"\ntimeout \"${3:-120}\" \"$godot\" --headless \"${fps_args[@]}\" --path godot --script \"res://tests/$1\" 2>&1 | tee \"$log\"\nstatus=$?\nif grep -qE \"SHADER ERROR|SCRIPT ERROR\" \"$log\"; then status=1; fi\nexit $status\ngodot/effects:\nembers.tscn\nembers_controller.gd\nembers_soft.png\nembers_soft.png.import\nhit_spark.tscn\nhit_spark_pool.gd\nhit_spark_pool.gd.uid\nhit_spark_star.png\nhit_spark_star.png.import\nmake_textures.gd\nmake_textures.gd.uid\n\ngodot/tests:\ncalibrate_normal_map.gd\ncalibrate_normal_map.gd.uid\ncapture_a5.gd\ncapture_a5.gd.uid\ncapture_flow.gd\ncapture_flow.gd.uid\ncapture_props3d.gd\ncapture_props3d.gd.uid\ncapture_states.gd\ncapture_states.gd.uid\ncheck_props3d.gd\ncheck_props3d.gd.uid\nnormal_map_check.gd\nnormal_map_check.gd.uid\ntest_embers_config.gd\ntest_embers_config.gd.uid\ntest_embers_state.gd\ntest_hit_spark_config.gd\ntest_hit_spark_config.gd.uid\ntest_hit_spark_state.gd\ntest_hit_spark_state.gd.uid\ntest_hurt_flash.gd\ntest_hurt_flash.gd.uid\ntest_materials.gd\ntest_materials.gd.uid\ntest_runner.gd\ntest_runner.gd.uid\n[gd_scene load_steps=11 format=3]\n\n[ext_resource type=\"Script\" path=\"res://game/main.gd\" id=\"1_main\"]\n[ext_resource type=\"Script\" path=\"res://game/stage.gd\" id=\"2_stage\"]\n[ext_resource type=\"PackedScene\" path=\"res://fighter/fighter.tscn\" id=\"3_fighter\"]\n[ext_resource type=\"Script\" path=\"res://game/effects.gd\" id=\"4_effects\"]\n[ext_resource type=\"Script\" path=\"res://game/hud.gd\" id=\"5_hud\"]\n[ext_resource type=\"Script\" path=\"res://game/audio_director.gd\" id=\"6_audio\"]\n[ext_resource type=\"PackedScene\" path=\"res://effects/hit_spark.tscn\" id=\"7_hit_spark\"]\n[ext_resource type=\"Script\" path=\"res://effects/hit_spark_pool.gd\" id=\"8_hit_spark_pool\"]\n[ext_resource type=\"PackedScene\" path=\"res://effects/embers.tscn\" id=\"9_embers\"]\n[ext_resource type=\"Script\" path=\"res://effects/embers_controller.gd\" id=\"10_embers_controller\"]\n\n[node name=\"Main\" type=\"Node2D\"]\nscript = ExtResource(\"1_main\")\n\n[node name=\"Stage\" type=\"Node2D\" parent=\".\"]\nscript = ExtResource(\"2_stage\")\n\n[node name=\"Embers\" parent=\".\" instance=ExtResource(\"9_embers\")]\n\n[node name=\"P1\" parent=\".\" instance=ExtResource(\"3_fighter\")]\nposition = Vector2(220, 305)\nfighter_id = \"akaken\"\ndisplay_name = \"AKAKEN\"\n\n[node name=\"P2\" parent=\".\" instance=ExtResource(\"3_fighter\")]\nposition = Vector2(420, 305)\nfighter_id = \"aotake\"\ndisplay_name = \"AOTAKE\"\n\n[node name=\"Effects\" type=\"Node2D\" parent=\".\"]\nscript = ExtResource(\"4_effects\")\n\n[node name=\"HitSpark0\" parent=\".\" instance=ExtResource(\"7_hit_spark\")]\n\n[node name=\"HitSpark1\" parent=\".\" instance=ExtResource(\"7_hit_spark\")]\n\n[node name=\"HitSpark2\" parent=\".\" instance=ExtResource(\"7_hit_spark\")]\n\n[node name=\"HitSpark3\" parent=\".\" instance=ExtResource(\"7_hit_spark\")]\n\n[node name=\"HitSparkPool\" type=\"Node\" parent=\".\"]\nscript = ExtResource(\"8_hit_spark_pool\")\n\n[node name=\"EmbersController\" type=\"Node\" parent=\".\"]\nscript = ExtResource(\"10_embers_controller\")\n\n[node name=\"HUD\" type=\"CanvasLayer\" parent=\".\"]\n\n[node name=\"Overlay\" type=\"Control\" parent=\"HUD\"]\nlayout_mode = 3\nanchors_preset = 15\nanchor_right = 1.0\nanchor_bottom = 1.0\ngrow_horizontal = 2\ngrow_vertical = 2\nmouse_filter = 2\nscript = ExtResource(\"5_hud\")\n\n[node name=\"AudioDirector\" type=\"Node\" parent=\".\"]\nscript = ExtResource(\"6_audio\")\nextends Node2D\n## Fight scene and round flow. Steps both fighters once per physics tick, resolves hits after both\n## have moved, keeps grounded fighters apart, and runs the phases from the storyboard:\n##   title (P1) -> intro \"ROUND n - FIGHT\" (P2) -> fight (P3-P5) -> ko (P6) -> result (P8)\n##   -> confirm = rematch (P7), Esc on the result screen = quit.\n## Pause (Esc/P) freezes the fight; M / N mute music / effects. Everything is stepped by step(),\n## so tests can drive it. Sound is handled by AudioDirector, which only listens to these signals.\n\nsignal round_started(round_number: int)\nsignal round_over(winner: Fighter)       # null on a double K.O.\nsignal paused_changed(paused: bool)\n\nconst INTRO_FRAMES := 60\nconst KO_FRAMES := 90           # input locked after K.O.; the winner poses at WIN_POSE_FRAME\nconst WIN_POSE_FRAME := 60\nconst HITSTOP_FRAMES := 4       # both fighters freeze briefly on a clean hit\n\n@onready var p1: Fighter = $P1\n@onready var p2: Fighter = $P2\n@onready var effects: Node2D = $Effects\n@onready var hud: Control = $HUD/Overlay\n@onready var audio: Node = $AudioDirector\n\nvar phase := \"title\"\nvar phase_frame := 0\nvar round_number := 0\nvar paused := false\nvar hitstop := 0\nvar winner: Fighter = null\nvar _message_before_pause := [\"\", \"\"]\n\n\nfunc _ready() -> void:\n\tp1.opponent = p2\n\tp2.opponent = p1\n\tp1.controller = PlayerController.new()\n\tp2.controller = CpuController.new()\n\thud.p1 = p1\n\thud.p2 = p2\n\thud.audio = audio\n\taudio.connect_game(self, [p1, p2])\n\tfor f in [p1, p2]:\n\t\tf.attack_resolved.connect(_on_attack_resolved)\n\t\tf.knocked_out.connect(_on_knocked_out)\n\tp1.reset(220.0, 1)\n\tp2.reset(420.0, -1)\n\t_show_title()\n\taudio.start_music()             # storyboard P1: the loop starts on the title screen\n\n\nfunc _physics_process(delta: float) -> void:\n\tstep(delta)\n\n\nfunc step(delta: float) -> void:\n\tif paused:\n\t\treturn\n\tphase_frame += 1\n\teffects.step()\n\tif hitstop > 0:\n\t\thitstop -= 1\n\t\treturn\n\tvar allow := phase == \"fight\"\n\tp1.step(delta, allow)\n\tp2.step(delta, allow)\n\tif phase == \"fight\" or phase == \"ko\":\n\t\tp1.check_hit()\n\t\tp2.check_hit()\n\t_separate()\n\tmatch phase:\n\t\t\"intro\":\n\t\t\tif phase_frame >= INTRO_FRAMES:\n\t\t\t\tphase = \"fight\"\n\t\t\t\thud.message = \"\"\n\t\t\"ko\":\n\t\t\tif phase_frame == WIN_POSE_FRAME and winner:\n\t\t\t\twinner.win()\n\t\t\tif phase_frame >= KO_FRAMES:\n\t\t\t\tphase = \"result\"\n\t\t\t\thud.message = \"%s WINS\" % winner.display_name if winner else \"DOUBLE K.O.\"\n\t\t\t\thud.sub_message = \"Enter: rematch     Esc: quit\"\n\n\n## Enter on the title or result screen.\nfunc confirm() -> void:\n\tif phase == \"title\" or phase == \"result\":\n\t\tstart_round()\n\n\nfunc start_round() -> void:\n\tround_number += 1\n\tp1.reset(220.0, 1)\n\tp2.reset(420.0, -1)\n\tp2.controller = CpuController.new(7270 + round_number)\n\teffects.clear()\n\twinner = null\n\thitstop = 0\n\tphase = \"intro\"\n\tphase_frame = 0\n\thud.message = \"ROUND %d  -  FIGHT\" % round_number\n\thud.sub_message = \"\"\n\tround_started.emit(round_number)\n\n\nfunc set_paused(value: bool) -> void:\n\tif value == paused or (value and phase != \"fight\" and phase != \"intro\"):\n\t\treturn\n\tpaused = value\n\tif paused:\n\t\t_message_before_pause = [hud.message, hud.sub_message]\n\t\thud.message = \"PAUSED\"\n\t\thud.sub_message = \"Esc / P: resume\"\n\telse:\n\t\thud.message = _message_before_pause[0]\n\t\thud.sub_message = _message_before_pause[1]\n\tpaused_changed.emit(paused)\n\n\n## For tests and the state capture: skip the title and intro.\nfunc start_fight_now() -> void:\n\tstart_round()\n\tphase = \"fight\"\n\thud.message = \"\"\n\n\nfunc _show_title() -> void:\n\tphase = \"title\"\n\thud.message = \"DUSK DUEL\"\n\thud.sub_message = \"press Enter\"\n\thud.hint = \"A/D move  W jump  S crouch  J punch  K kick  L block  Esc pause  M/N mute  F1 boxes\"\n\n\nfunc _on_attack_resolved(f: Fighter, _kind: String, result: String, point: Vector2) -> void:\n\tif result == \"interrupted\":\n\t\treturn\n\teffects.spawn(result, point, f.facing)\n\tif result == \"hit\":\n\t\thitstop = HITSTOP_FRAMES\n\n\nfunc _on_knocked_out(_loser: Fighter) -> void:\n\tif phase == \"ko\":\n\t\twinner = null if (p1.state == \"ko\" and p2.state == \"ko\") else winner\n\t\treturn\n\tphase = \"ko\"\n\tphase_frame = 0\n\twinner = p2 if p1.state == \"ko\" else p1\n\thud.message = \"K.O.\"\n\thud.sub_message = \"\"\n\tround_over.emit(winner)\n\n\n## Grounded fighters push each other apart; jumping over the opponent is allowed.\nfunc _separate() -> void:\n\tif not (p1.is_grounded() and p2.is_grounded()) or p1.state == \"ko\" or p2.state == \"ko\":\n\t\treturn\n\tvar min_gap := p1.body_half_width() + p2.body_half_width()\n\tvar dx := p2.position.x - p1.position.x\n\tif absf(dx) >= min_gap:\n\t\treturn\n\tvar push := (min_gap - absf(dx)) / 2.0\n\tvar dir := signf(dx) if dx != 0.0 else 1.0\n\tp1.position.x = clampf(p1.position.x - dir * push, Fighter.ARENA_LEFT, Fighter.ARENA_RIGHT)\n\tp2.position.x = clampf(p2.position.x + dir * push, Fighter.ARENA_LEFT, Fighter.ARENA_RIGHT)\n\n\nfunc _unhandled_input(event: InputEvent) -> void:\n\tif event.is_action_pressed(\"confirm\"):\n\t\tconfirm()\n\telif event.is_action_pressed(\"pause\"):\n\t\tif phase == \"result\":\n\t\t\tget_tree().quit()\n\t\telse:\n\t\t\tset_paused(not paused)\n\telif event.is_action_pressed(\"mute_music\"):\n\t\taudio.toggle_mute(\"Music\")\n\telif event.is_action_pressed(\"mute_sfx\"):\n\t\taudio.toggle_mute(\"SFX\")\n\telif event.is_action_pressed(\"debug_boxes\"):\n\t\tfor f in [p1, p2]:\n\t\t\tf.show_boxes = not f.show_boxes\n\t\t\tf.queue_redraw()","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,